{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\nPlan review LLM calls run at the flat DEFAULT_MAX_TOKENS (16000, src/rebar/llm/config.py:269) with no output-budget raise anywhere in the plan-review call sites. A structured response that exceeds the ceiling raises UnretryableOutputError (src/rebar/llm/structured.py; runner.py:628-651 degrades to INDETERMINATE) — observed live on epic a492's container review: one bin over 17 children failed after 333s, and the S7-landed exhaustiveness directive (enumerate every independent defect in one run) deliberately increases per-call finding output, widening this exposure. Truncation here has only bad outcomes: a full-cost re-review or silent loss of critical findings. The completion verifier was remediated for the same family by RAISING the output token budget (completion_recovery.py raises max_tokens, :207/:222); plan review needs the comparable remediation. Operator goal: allow effectively unlimited output tokens for plan-review calls — output is naturally bounded by the model's actual findings, and unspent max_tokens costs nothing.\n\n## Approach\nRaise every plan-review LLM call's output budget to the RESOLVED MODEL'S MAXIMUM output capacity (the API requires a finite max_tokens, so model-max IS the unlimited setting). Mechanism: the runner already lets a request raise the config floor (runner.effective_max_tokens — a request may only raise, and req.output_token_limit still clamps down where bounded recovery needs it). Add a per-model max-output lookup — check first whether the just-landed ModelProfile capabilities seam (change 1014, f184: read capabilities from ModelProfile) exposes max output tokens and use it; otherwise a small table beside sizing.largest_window_tokens with a conservative fallback to the current default for unknown models. Apply it at the plan-review request builders: Pass-1 finder chunks and AGENT criteria, container bins, ISF finder/summarizer, prerequisite finder, and the verify/coach workflow steps (whichever do not already scale via output_tokens_per_item — the verify agentic arm's existing per-item scaling and 64000 ceiling may be replaced by or reconciled with model-max; state the final rule uniformly). Bounded-recovery paths that intentionally clamp via output_token_limit are untouched. Verify timeout interaction: larger max_tokens must not trip request timeouts (cfg.timeout_s; the SDK's streaming requirement for long requests is handled at the transport — confirm by reading anthropic_model.py). Alternative rejected: per-bin child-count scaling (this ticket's earlier draft) — still an arbitrary ceiling; any finite budget below model-max re-creates the truncation class the operator ruled out.\n\n## Scope\nsrc/rebar/llm/plan_review/passes.py (request builders), src/rebar/llm/plan_review/sizing.py (or the ModelProfile seam: model max-output lookup), src/rebar/llm/workflow/gates/plan-review.yaml (verify/coach step budgets reconciled), tests/unit/workflow/test_plan_review_output_budget.py (new), tests updated where they pin request max_tokens.\n\n## Testing\nUnit with a recording FakeRunner: every plan-review request carries max_tokens equal to the resolved model's max output (per the lookup) and never below DEFAULT_MAX_TOKENS; unknown model falls back to the default; output_token_limit clamps still apply where set; the verify arm's budget follows the stated final rule; existing plan-review workflow tests pass.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] All Pass-1 (chunk, AGENT, container, ISF, prerequisite) plan-review requests carry the resolved model's maximum output budget, floor-raised through the existing runner contract (checked: `pytest tests/unit/workflow/test_plan_review_output_budget.py` asserting request fields for each call type).\n- [ ] Unknown/unmapped models fall back to the current default without error (checked: unit test).\n- [ ] Bounded-recovery output_token_limit clamps are unaffected (checked: existing recovery tests pass).\n- [ ] A synthetic oversized-findings container fixture that previously raised UnretryableOutputError at 16000 completes under the raised budget (checked: unit test with a FakeRunner that enforces the request ceiling)."}},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1785477330160685001,"uuid":"ef7c2626-ab4a-4584-a62a-0454267c4afc"}